Another limitation is that EUREKA requires a task fitness function F to exist and easily definable by humans. While this assumption holds for a wide range of robot tasks (including all our benchmark tasks) and is required for reward design problem to be well-defined (Definition 2.1), there are certain behavior that is hard to specify mathematically, such as “running in a stable gait”. In those cases, we have presented EUREKA from Human Feedback (Section 4.4) that uses human textual feedback to directly steer the reward generation, sidestepping having to specify F that accurately captures the human intent. A promising future work direction is to use vision-language models (VLMs) to automatically provide textual feedback by feeding the policy videos into the VLMs (Liu et al., 2023b;
Zhu et al., 2023; Yang et al., 2023).

